				<h4>About author</h4> 
					Carson Ellis is an acclaimed American illustrator and author, globally celebrated for her distinctive, folk-art-inspired aesthetic and whimsical storytelling. Best known for illustrating bestselling children's books and novels like Wildwood (written by her husband, Colin Meloy), The Mysterious Benedict Society series, and Lemony Snicket's The Composer Is Dead, as well as writing and illustrating her own celebrated picture books such as Home and Du Iz Tak? (a Caldecott Honor Book), she masterfully combines intricate botanical details, muted earth tones, and imaginative world-building, consistently creating enchanting works that captivate readers of all ages.				
